===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|حجب|tr=ħájaba||to veil, to cover, to screen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hɪˈdʒɑːb/|/hɪˈdʒæb/|lang=en}}<ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref>
* {{rhymes|ɑːb|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|uncountable|Islam|lang=en}} The practice, among Muslim women, of covering the body after the [[age]] of [[puberty]] in front of non-related [[adult]] [[males]].
#* '''2010''', Jawairriya Abdallah-Shahid, ''Veiled Voices'' (ISBN 1450053025), page 13:
#*: The belief that Muslim females observe '''hijab''' because men force them to do so insults some Muslim females who have based their decision on their understanding of Islam.
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A traditional [[headscarf]] worn by Muslim women, covering the hair and neck.

